462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 193 0 R
/T (How a dictionary finds a key. Python calculates hash\(key\) and uses it to choose a slot in an internal array. If the slot holds an equal key, the value is returned directly; if another key occupies it \(a collision\), a short probe sequence is followed. The table is resized when it gets too full, so chains stay short and the average lookup cost is O\(1\) whatever the number of keys. )
/E (How a dictionary finds a key. Python calculates hash\(key\) and uses it to choose a slot in an internal array. If the slot holds an equal key, the value is returned directly; if another key occupies it \(a collision\), a short probe sequence is followed. The table is resized when it gets too full, so chains stay short and the average lookup cost is O\(1\) whatever the number of keys. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
