/T (Engineering decision. For 100,000 complaints a day I would deploy a dictionary-based count, using collections.Counter if no special cleaning is needed. Both are O\(n\) with time of a few hundredths of a second; list.count\(\) grows with the number of distinct words and is unsuitable. Counter is shorter and well tested; the explicit dictionary loop is better when each word needs custom cleaning. )
