/T (General form. [expression for item in iterable if condition]. Here: [c for c in readings if -50 <= c <= 50]. Comprehension or loop. A comprehension becomes harder to read than a loop when it has several nested for clauses, several conditions, or needs more than one statement \(for example logging a rejected reading\). The loop version is then clearer. )
/E (General form. [expression for item in iterable if condition]. Here: [c for c in readings if -50 <= c <= 50]. Comprehension or loop. A comprehension becomes harder to read than a loop when it has several nested for clauses, several conditions, or needs more than one statement \(for example logging a rejected reading\). The loop version is then clearer. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
