/Title (How a dictionary finds a key. Python calculates hash\(key\) and uses it to choose a slot in an internal array. If the slot holds an equal key, the value is returned directly; if another key occupies it \(a collision\), a short probe sequence is followed. The table is resized when it gets too full, so chains stay short and the average lookup cost is O\(1\) whatever the number of keys.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1983 0 R
/Next 1997 0 R
