<<
/Title (Engineering decision. For 100,000 complaints a day I would deploy a dictionary-based count, using collections.Counter if no special cleaning is needed. Both are O\(n\) with time of a few hundredths of a second; list.count\(\) grows with the number of distinct words and is unsuitable. Counter is shorter and well tested; the explicit dictionary loop is better when each word needs custom cleaning.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1983 0 R
/Prev 2004 0 R
/Next 1990 0 R
>>
endobj
