2008 0 obj
<<
/Title (Alarm minutes. enumerate\(\) supplies the minute number with each reading: [m for m, c in enumerate\(readings\) if valid and not 2 <= c <= 8]. Invalid sensor readings are not counted as alarms. List comprehension versus generator expression. A list comprehension builds the whole list in memory at once. A generator expression \(round brackets\) produces one value at a time when asked, stores nothing, and can be read only once. The measurements show 6,675,480 bytes for the list and 208 bytes for the generator object.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1995 0 R
/Prev 2007 0 R
/Next 2002 0 R
>>
endobj
2009 0 obj
<<
/Title (Dictionary order. From Python 3.7 a dictionary keeps keys in insertion order \(guaranteed by the language\). Re-assigning an existing key does not change its position.)
